.Dd November 22, 2026
.Dt PROWLCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm prowlctl
.Nd control utility for prowld(8)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar rundir
.Op Fl \-json
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the command-line interface for
.Xr prowld 8 .
It connects to the
.Xr prowld 8
control socket at
.Pa /var/run/prowld/prowld.sock
and sends commands over the JSON IPC protocol.
Most commands require appropriate privilege;
operations that modify service state or system configuration
must be run as root.
.Pp
The following global options are available:
.Bl -tag -width "--json"
.It Fl s Ar rundir
Connect to the
.Xr prowld 8
that was started with
.Fl s Ar rundir ,
that is to
.Pa rundir/prowld.sock ,
instead of the system one.
It must come first, before any other option or the command.
.It Fl \-json
Print raw JSON responses instead of human-readable output.
Useful for scripts and monitoring tools.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
Where a command takes a
.Ar label ,
an instance of a template unit may be given as a second word instead of after an
.Dq @ :
.Dq "prowlctl start dhclient wlan0"
is
.Dq "prowlctl start dhclient@wlan0" .
.Bl -tag -width "reload-config"
.It Cm list Op Fl \-enabled | Fl \-failed | Fl \-type Ns = Ns Ar type
List known jobs.
With no filter options all loaded jobs are shown regardless of state.
The filters are applied by
.Xr prowld 8
and can be combined; a job is shown only if it passes all of them.
.Fl \-enabled
shows only jobs that are enabled: not disabled in
.Xr rc.conf 5
and not masked.
.Fl \-failed
shows only jobs currently in the
.Dv failed
state.
.Fl \-type Ns = Ns Ar type
shows only jobs of that type; valid values are
.Cm daemon ,
.Cm oneshot ,
.Cm timer ,
.Cm socket
and
.Cm rcshim .
Any other value is an error.
.It Cm status Ar label
Show detailed status for a single job, including its state, PID,
restart count, last exit code, and any status message reported via
sd_notify
.Pq Dv STATUS=... .
.Ar label
may be either the full unit label
.Pq e.g., Dq org.midnightbsd.sshd
or the short rc_name
.Pq e.g., Dq sshd .
.It Cm start Ar label
Start the named job.
The job must be loaded and not currently running.
If the job has unsatisfied hard dependencies the command will fail.
.It Cm stop Ar label
Stop the named job.
.Xr prowld 8
sends
.Dv SIGTERM
and waits up to
.Va exit_timeout
seconds for the process to exit before sending
.Dv SIGKILL .
.Pp
A legacy
.Xr rc.d 8
script
.Pq an rcshim job
whose start has finished has no process of its own, because the script
started a daemon and exited.
For such a job
.Xr prowld 8
runs the script's
.Cm stop
instead, with the same time limit.
.It Cm restart Ar label
Stop then start the named job again, once it has stopped.
This also starts a job that is stopped, completed or failed.
.It Cm reload Ar label
Make the named job re-read its configuration.
If the unit defines
.Va reload_arguments
that command is run and its output is printed, and
.Nm
exits with its exit status.
Otherwise
.Dv SIGHUP
is sent to the job, which by convention causes a daemon to re-read its
configuration without dropping connections.
The job must be in the
.Dv running
or
.Dv completed
state.
.It Cm check Ar label
Run the unit's
.Va check_arguments
command, which tests the configuration without applying it, and print its
output.
.Nm
exits with the command's exit status.
The job does not have to be running.
.It Cm resync Ar label
Run the unit's
.Va resync_arguments
command, which brings the running service back in line with its
configuration, for example by reloading firewall rules.
The job must be running or completed.
.It Cm enable Ar label
Mark a job to start at boot by setting
.Va \*(Lt rc_name \*(Gt _enable=YES
in
.Pa /etc/rc.conf
via
.Xr sysrc 8 .
For unit jobs that do not have an rc_name the job's label is used.
.It Cm disable Ar label
Mark a job to not start at boot by setting
.Va \*(Lt rc_name \*(Gt _enable=NO
in
.Pa /etc/rc.conf .
Does not stop a currently running instance.
.It Cm mask Ar label
Unconditionally prevent a job from starting even as a dependency.
Creates a placeholder file in
.Pa /var/db/prowld/masked.d/ .
Masking stops a running job, closes its activation sockets, and
prevents manual, dependency, and timer starts while the mask is present.
If
.Pa /var
is a separate file system, early boot jobs can start before their saved
masks become available.
.Xr prowld 8
rechecks the masks after the file systems are mounted.
.It Cm unmask Ar label
Remove a mask created by
.Cm mask .
The job becomes eligible for its configured activation sources again.
.It Cm show Ar label
Dump the effective configuration of a job as a JSON object.
The output reflects all parsed unit-file fields and runtime defaults.
Useful for verifying that a unit file was parsed correctly.
.It Cm reload-config
Rescan all unit directories and
.Xr rc.d 8
script directories for new or changed files,
then rebuild the dependency graph.
Running jobs are not stopped or restarted.
Equivalent to sending
.Dv SIGHUP
to
.Xr prowld 8
directly.
.It Cm shutdown
Ask
.Xr prowld 8
to shut down, and wait until it has exited.
It stops the jobs, and when
.Xr prowld 8
is the service manager of a jail it first runs
.Pa /etc/rc.shutdown .
Intended as the
.Va exec.stop
command of a jail whose
.Va exec.start
is
.Pa /sbin/prowld ;
see
.Xr prowld 8 .
It is refused when
.Xr prowld 8
is
.Xr init 8 ,
which must be stopped with
.Xr shutdown 8
or
.Xr reboot 8 .
.It Cm daemon-reexec
Re-execute
.Xr prowld 8
in place without disturbing running services.
Intended for upgrading the daemon binary while the system is live.
The new process inherits all open file descriptors and job state.
.It Cm dependencies Ar label
Show the dependency list for a job.
Each entry names the dependency and whether it is a hard
.Pq Cm requires
or soft
.Pq Cm wants
dependency.
.It Cm graph Op Fl \-format Ns = Ns Ar fmt
Emit the full service dependency graph.
Without options, output is a human-readable edge table showing
each job and its direct dependencies.
With
.Fl \-format Ns = Ns Ar dot ,
output is Graphviz DOT format suitable for rendering with
.Xr dot 1 .
.It Cm logs Ar label Op Fl \-follow Op Fl \-lines Ns = Ns Ar N
Display the captured log output for a job.
Only available for jobs whose unit sets
.Va standard_out_path
or
.Va standard_error_path
to
.Pa /var/log/prowld/jobs/ Ns Ar label Ns Pa .log ;
see
.Xr prowl-unit 5 .
None of the units in the base system do.
.Pp
.Ar label
may be the full label or any name the other commands accept, such as
.Dq sshd
or
.Dq dhclient@em0 ;
.Nm
asks
.Xr prowld 8
for the full label.
A name
.Xr prowld 8
does not know is used as given, so the log of a job that has been
removed can still be read.
.Pp
.Fl \-follow
tails the file continuously, similar to
.Xr tail 1
.Fl f .
Use
.Ic ^C
to stop following.
.Fl \-lines Ns = Ns Ar N
limits initial output to the last
.Ar N
lines; the default is 50.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
Additional exit codes:
.Bl -tag -width "3" -compact
.It 1
Job not found or invalid label.
.It 2
Job is in a failed state and the operation could not be performed.
.It 3
Operation not permitted (insufficient privilege).
.It 4
.Xr prowld 8
is not running or not responding on the control socket.
.Nm
gives up when
.Xr prowld 8
has not answered for 30 seconds.
For
.Cm check , reload ,
and
.Cm resync ,
the client waits up to 40 seconds so that the daemon can return the
result of its 30-second action timeout.
The operation may still be carried out.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
List all loaded services:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
prowlctl list
.Ed
.Pp
Show only failed services:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
prowlctl list --failed
.Ed
.Pp
Start the SSH daemon:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
prowlctl start org.midnightbsd.sshd
.Ed
.Pp
Enable a service at boot:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
prowlctl enable sshd
.Ed
.Pp
Check detailed status, using short rc name:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
prowlctl status sshd
.Ed
.Pp
Follow a service's log output:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
prowlctl logs org.midnightbsd.nginx --follow
.Ed
.Pp
Render the dependency graph as a PDF:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
prowlctl graph --format=dot | dot -Tpdf -o deps.pdf
.Ed
.Pp
Get machine-readable status for scripting:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
prowlctl --json status org.midnightbsd.sshd | jq .state
.Ed
.Pp
Mask a unit to prevent it from ever starting:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
prowlctl mask org.midnightbsd.bluetooth
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It "prowld not running or socket unavailable"
.Xr prowld 8
is not started, or the control socket at
.Pa /var/run/prowld/prowld.sock
does not exist.
Start prowld or check
.Pa /var/log/prowld/prowld.log
for startup errors.
If prowld was started with a custom run directory via
.Fl s ,
the socket will be under that directory instead.
.It "operation not permitted"
The command requires root privilege.
Re-run with
.Xr su 1 ,
.Xr doas 1 ,
or
.Xr sudo 8
if installed.
.It "job not found: \*(Ltlabel\*(Gt"
No loaded job matches the given label or rc_name.
Run
.Cm prowlctl list
to see all known jobs and confirm the spelling.
If the unit file was recently added, run
.Cm prowlctl reload-config
first.
.It "job is masked"
The job has been masked with
.Cm prowlctl mask
and cannot be started.
Use
.Cm prowlctl unmask Ar label
to remove the mask.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/log/prowld/jobs/<label>.log" -compact
.It Pa /var/run/prowld/prowld.sock
.Xr prowld 8
control socket.
If prowld was started with
.Fl s Ar rundir ,
the socket is at
.Pa Ar rundir Ns /prowld.sock
instead.
.It Pa /var/db/prowld/masked.d/
Directory of mask files created by
.Cm prowlctl mask .
.It Pa /var/log/prowld/jobs/ Ns Ar label Ns Pa .log
Per-job log file, read by
.Cm prowlctl logs .
.It Pa /etc/rc.conf
Modified by
.Cm enable
and
.Cm disable
via
.Xr sysrc 8 .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr doas 1 ,
.Xr su 1 ,
.Xr tail 1 ,
.Xr dot 1 ,
.Xr prowl-unit 5 ,
.Xr rc 8 ,
.Xr service 8 ,
.Xr sysrc 8 ,
.Xr prowld 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in MidnightBSD 4.1.
